# Route outsource + always-approve (skill contract)

**Canon skill:** `.cursor/skills/route/SKILL.md` (CCC / user-global).
**Canon scripts:** private `cemini23/agent-toolkit` (`~/Projects/agent-toolkit`, `ROUTE_KIT`, or `/opt/cemini/agent-toolkit` on prod). TipDrop kit redirects only.

Always-approve is the default on **every** executor on **every** machine. This is the **base-case task router for all Cemini work** (Atto, CCC, OSINT, TipDrop, wikis) — not a TipDrop-only workflow.

## Goal

Minimize Cursor Agent spend. Prefer OpenRouter free → claude-ds Flash; mid = Grok plan + claude-ds Flash; hard = Cursor premium plan + Grok CLI implement. **Grok CLI usage out:** claude-ds Pro stands in (mid plan / hard implement). One harness; `-Model` selects Flash vs Pro.

## When user says `/route`, `route this`, `route as recommended`, or asks to outsource

1. Announce lane (easy/mid/hard/money) in one line.
2. **Shell out** to `route-task` / `agent-toolkit/scripts/route-task.ps1` from the **current project** (or `-WorkDir`). Do **not** implement in the parent Cursor session (except Cursor Grok fallback when the script says so).
3. **Hard/money:** write the premium plan into the handoff `## Plan` first (SIP), then shell Grok implement (or claude-ds Pro when Grok usage is out).
4. Summarize executor results only — include verify evidence / SDR; no status-only "done".

## WorkDir

Default = current project directory. TipDrop scanner only when the task is clearly scanner/TipDrop work. Never assume TipDrop cwd for Atto/CCC/OSINT/etc.

## Always-approve defaults (all profiles / all hosts)

- Grok: `--always-approve` (opt out `-NoApprove` on that run only)
- claude-ds: `--dangerously-skip-permissions` (opt out `CLAUDE_DS_ASK=1` / `-NoSkipPermissions`)
- Cursor Grok / Cursor Agent fallback: Auto-run — still no LIVE Discord / no secret paste
- One-time machine adopt: `pwsh -File ~/Projects/agent-toolkit/scripts/adopt-route-always-approve.ps1`
- **Grok login/auth failure:** tell operator to `grok login` (or set `XAI_API_KEY`). Auth is not usage-out. **Grok usage/quota out:** mid → claude-ds Pro plans then Flash executes; hard + Plan → claude-ds Pro implements; then Cursor Grok if Pro also fails.

## Profiles

- `david` / `claudio` — logging / future local opts; easy chain is OpenRouter free → claude-ds for both
- Env: `ROUTE_PROFILE` (aliases `CEMINI_ROUTE_PROFILE`, `TIPDROP_ROUTE_PROFILE`)
- Always-approve does **not** vary by profile

## Safety unchanged

No secrets in handoffs. No secrets on free OpenRouter models. No LIVE Discord without LIVE OK.
